\textbf{Solution.} Earthing sets $V_B=0$, but does not by itself change the currents. The three equal resistors share 6 V equally, so each drop is 2 V. Starting from the positive terminal ($+6$ V), the potential decreases by 2 V after each resistor: $+4$ V at $P$, $+2$ V at $Q$, and $0$ V at $B$.
\end{exercise}

